From 164bef4fa331cbbc6c64528651cee149e1e4f139 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nathan <nsafran1217@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 20:54:38 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] sn2: call sn_timer_interrupt() from the timer tick again

Until 5.4, timer_interrupt() called platform_timer_interrupt(), which
was sn_timer_interrupt() on SN2.  The call went away with the machvec
infrastructure and the SN2 restore never put it back, so
sn_timer_interrupt() has had no caller.  That silently disabled:

 - sn_lb_int_war_check(), SGI's lost-interrupt workaround for PIC
   bridges behind SHub1: every 100 ticks each CPU checks its PIC IRQs
   for an interrupt that the PIC has sent but the CPU never saw, and
   forces it again;
 - the SHub 1.1 PIO workaround write to pio_shub_war_cam_addr;
 - the heartbeat LED.

Call it where 4.19 did, before the tick is accounted.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
---
 arch/ia64/kernel/time.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/ia64/kernel/time.c b/arch/ia64/kernel/time.c
index ec46c6eab7f7..5dad41e50c45 100644
--- a/arch/ia64/kernel/time.c
+++ b/arch/ia64/kernel/time.c
@@ -180,6 +180,13 @@ timer_interrupt (int irq, void *dev_id)
 		return IRQ_HANDLED;
 	}
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_IA64_SGI_SN2
+	{
+		extern void sn_timer_interrupt(int irq, void *dev_id);
+		sn_timer_interrupt(irq, dev_id);
+	}
+#endif
+
 	new_itm = local_cpu_data->itm_next;
 
 	if (!time_after(ia64_get_itc(), new_itm))
-- 
